From 5fcc18b23677e8f6415f0d432d9ac1b84b1541e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio Fantoni <fantonifabio@tiscali.it>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:37:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] csm-systemd.c: Take the session's logind inhibitor in
 block-weak mode when available.

Since systemd 257, logind always obeys "block" inhibitors, including the
ones held by the user who requests the operation (before, those were
ignored for the same user and for root). The "sleep:shutdown" inhibitor
that cinnamon-session takes on behalf of applications inhibiting suspend
(Rhythmbox while playing, browsers playing media, ...) now blocks the
session itself:

- closing the lid: csd-power locks the screen and calls Suspend(), which
is refused, so the laptop stays on;
- end-session dialog: logind answers "inhibited" to
CanSuspend/CanPowerOff/CanReboot, so suspend, restart and shut down are
not offered, and "Ignore and continue" for suspend does nothing.

The "block-weak" mode, added in systemd 257, keeps the previous
semantics. Suspend on idle still honours the inhibitors, since csd-power
checks the session inhibitors itself before arming the sleep timeout.
gnome-session did the same (39d51c9e6, "systemd: Downgrade suspend
inhibitor to block-weak").

systemd-logind and elogind older than 257 don't know "block-weak": there
the inhibitor is still taken in "block" mode, which on those versions is
ignored for the same user anyway. The BlockWeakInhibited property, added
together with the new mode, tells the two apart.

Ref: https://github.com/linuxmint/cinnamon/issues/13219

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/linuxmint/cinnamon-session/pull/219 (commit 5fcc18b23677e8f6415f0d432d9ac1b84b1541e9)
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
---
 cinnamon-session/csm-systemd.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cinnamon-session/csm-systemd.c b/cinnamon-session/csm-systemd.c
index bd6a70b..3ade9ca 100644
--- a/cinnamon-session/csm-systemd.c
+++ b/cinnamon-session/csm-systemd.c
@@ -684,19 +684,27 @@ csm_systemd_add_inhibitor (CsmSystem        *system,
                            CsmInhibitorFlag  flag)
 {
         CsmSystemd *manager = CSM_SYSTEMD (system);
+        GVariant *block_weak;
+        const gchar *mode;
 
         if ((flag & CSM_INHIBITOR_FLAG_SUSPEND) == 0)
                 return;
 
         if (manager->priv->inhibitors == NULL) {
-                g_debug ("Adding system inhibitor");
+                /* Since 257, logind obeys "block" even for the user holding it;
+                 * older versions don't know "block-weak" nor this property. */
+                block_weak = g_dbus_proxy_get_cached_property (manager->priv->sd_proxy, "BlockWeakInhibited");
+                mode = block_weak != NULL ? "block-weak" : "block";
+                g_clear_pointer (&block_weak, g_variant_unref);
+
+                g_debug ("Adding system inhibitor (%s)", mode);
                 g_dbus_proxy_call_with_unix_fd_list (manager->priv->sd_proxy,
                                                      "Inhibit",
                                                      g_variant_new ("(ssss)",
                                                                     "sleep:shutdown",
                                                                     g_get_user_name (),
                                                                     "user session inhibited",
-                                                                    "block"),
+                                                                    mode),
                                                      0,
                                                      G_MAXINT,
                                                      NULL,
